A||||2||maffthekat||Melted harness||||11||
Z||000000||maffthekat||07-13-2001||04:08 AM||||Peering into my engine compartment the other day I noticed that one of the wiring harnesses at the back (the large one in the centre) has been melted down one side and the wires look thicker where the insulation has expanded in the heat. It was like that when I got the car honest!<BR>Everything seemed to be working alright in the car electrically, until the computer complained about my TPS with a error 21 so I replaced it with a new one and now when I turn the ignition on the 'check engine' light stays on and the computer still reports a TPS error but with code 22.<BR>Is it easy to get a replacement harness and if so is it a nightmare to install it?||||reg||11
Z||000001||84Bill||07-13-2001||08:29 AM||||Not really. <BR>It can be a pain to thread the harness around stuff while the engine is in the car but it's not impossible. Give yourself plenty of time to do the job and don't be in a hurry. I have done it several times now and it's becoume routine.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||07-13-2001||10:28 AM||||did you unhook the battery to clear the original error code? they stay there till the battery is disconnected - your ECM doesnt know you replaced the sensor until you do.||||reg||1
